## Viewer pattern
```csharp
private readonly Viewer<MyScreenView> _myScreenViewer;

public MyController(MyScreenView prefab)
{
    _myScreenViewer = new(prefab);
}

public void Open(RectTransform container)
{
    var view = _myScreenViewer.ShowExpand(container);
    view.Display();
    view.AnimateShow();
}
```

## GameState pattern
```csharp
public class GameState : MonoBehaviour, IGameState
{
    int IGameState.Version => 1;

    void IGameState.Parse(Dictionary<string, string> data)
    {
        IGameState.ParseState(data);
        // parse custom keys here
    }

    Dictionary<string, string> IGameState.ToDictionary()
    {
        var result = new Dictionary<string, string>();
        result.Add(IGameState.GetStateDictionary());
        return result;
    }

    bool IGameState.TransferParsingAvailable => false;
    Dictionary<string, string> IGameState.TransferParse(string data) => throw new NotImplementedException();
}
```

## Built-in DevNote state and API
- `IGameState` already contains `NoAdsPurchased`, `SaveVersion`, `PurchasedPermanentProducts`, `LastOnlineTime`, `IsFirstLaunch`.
- `IEnvironment` uses `UtcTime`, `DeviceLanguage`, `DeviceType`, fullscreen API, invite API, and channel mute API.
- `IRemote` throws if `SetDefaultHandler()` was not called before reading a key.
- `IPurchase` automatically tracks bought permanent products in `IGameState.PurchasedPermanentProducts`.
- `IAds` statuses: `Success`, `NoAdsPurchased`, `AdBlockEnabled`, `CooldownNotFinished`, `Error`.
- `ILeaderboards` uses `SetScore()` and `OpenLeaderboard()`.
- `IAnalytics` uses `SendEvent(string, Dictionary<string, object>)`.
- `IReview` uses `ReviewIsAvailable` and `Rate(...)`.

## Saves and sound
- WebGL cannot reliably save on close, so periodic `SaveLocal` is required.
- Use `FullSave` / `SaveCloud` on important milestones, not after every small action.
- `Viewer<T>` lazy-loads its prefab in current DevNote.
- `SoundUnit` stores an Addressables reference to `AudioClip`; prefer access through project configs such as `Configs.AudioHub.Show.Play()`.

## Rule split
- Keep `devnote_main.mdc` as the always-on rule.
- Use this file for details, examples, and low-frequency API reminders.
